{"name":"Rosemary White","hex":"#dfe3db","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosemary","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub, Salvia rosmarinus (formerly Rosmarinus officinalis), that originates from Europe and Asia Minor and produces a fragrant herb used in cooking and perfumes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosemary"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of Home and Away characters introduced in 1989","blocks":[{"text":"Home and Away is an Australian television soap opera. It was first broadcast on the Seven Network on 17 January 1988. The following is a list of characters that first appeared in 1989, by order of first appearance. They were all introduced by the show's executive producer Des Monaghan. The 2nd season of Home and Away began airing on 23 January 1989. The first introduction of the year was Martha Stewart in January. Nana Coburn made her first appearance as schoolgirl Vicki Baxter the following month. Rebecca Fisher made her first appearance in April. Emily Symons joined the cast as Marilyn Chambers in May. In June, the serial saw the birth of Duncan Stewart, the first child of Alf and Ailsa. Mat Stevenson took on the role of Adam Cameron a fortnight later. Mouche Phillips joined as Viv Newton in July, and September saw the arrival of Dannii Minogue as Emma Jackson."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Home_and_Away_characters_introduced_in_1989"},{"title":"Rosemary","blocks":[{"text":"Salvia rosmarinus, synonym Rosmarinus officinalis, commonly known as rosemary, is a shrub with fragrant, evergreen, needle-like leaves and purple or sometimes white, pink, or blue flowers. It is a member of the mint family, Lamiaceae. The species is native to the Mediterranean region. It has numerous cultivars, and its leaves are commonly used as a flavoring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Rosemary_in_bloom.JPG/330px-Rosemary_in_bloom.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosemary"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/RosemarySprig.jpg/500px-RosemarySprig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/RosemarySprig.jpg/1280px-RosemarySprig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/RosemarySprig.jpg/500px-RosemarySprig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rosemary leaves","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosemarySprig.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Rosmarinus_officinalis_prostratus.jpg/500px-Rosmarinus_officinalis_prostratus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Rosmarinus_officinalis_prostratus.jpg/1280px-Rosmarinus_officinalis_prostratus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Rosmarinus_officinalis_prostratus.jpg/500px-Rosmarinus_officinalis_prostratus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"S. rosmarinus 'Prostratus'","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosmarinus_officinalis_prostratus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Salvia_rosmarinus_MHNT.BOT.2023.13.45.jpg/500px-Salvia_rosmarinus_MHNT.BOT.2023.13.45.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Salvia_rosmarinus_MHNT.BOT.2023.13.45.jpg/1280px-Salvia_rosmarinus_MHNT.BOT.2023.13.45.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Salvia_rosmarinus_MHNT.BOT.2023.13.45.jpg/500px-Salvia_rosmarinus_MHNT.BOT.2023.13.45.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross-section of woody stem of Salvia rosmarinus (MHNT)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalvia_rosmarinus_MHNT.BOT.2023.13.45.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Rosemary_Plant.jpg/500px-Rosemary_Plant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Rosemary_Plant.jpg/1280px-Rosemary_Plant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Rosemary_Plant.jpg/500px-Rosemary_Plant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe